  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality\n$({e}^{2x}+{x}^{4})(5x-1)<0.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since ${e}^{2x}+{x}^{4}$ is always positive, we can divide both sides of the inequality by this quantity. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({e}^{2x}+{x}^{4})(5x-1)}{{e}^{2x}+{x}^{4}} & <\\frac{0}{{e}^{2x}+{x}^{4}} \\\\ 5x-1 & <0 \\\\ 5x & <1 \\\\ x & <\\,\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
